In article <4587.27525474@cc.nu.oz.au> c8730752@cc.nu.oz.au writes:
>i found a 1 charge blessed wow in the castle and recharged it once before, 
>also 1 charge. then used another blessed scroll of charging and the wow 
>exploded! why is that? 

I know for a fact that wands of wishing can only be recharged once, and I
believe that wands in general can only ever be recharged once.  Always use
a blessed scroll of charging, as that will recharge the wand to its
maximum charges (3 in the case of a wand of wishing).

>a wand of polymorph of zero charge i left for some time, was then picked up
>by a dragon, i zap it after despatching the dragon and there was one more zap 
>and then it exploded...is there a clue in this? or does wow simply explode
>on the 3rd charging?

Wands in general can be zapped one more time after the charges are down to 
zero.  This takes a lot of patience, however - keep trying.  The one 
problem is that squeezing this one last charge out of the wand will always
cause it to explode, so make sure you've gotten all the other charges you
could out of it (i.e. zap it dry, blessed charge it, zap it dry, and then
squeeze the one last charge out).

>BTW, why does crystal balls need charges to work? does it not depend on the
>crystal-gazer and not the crystal ball as in fortune telling?

Treat it like a TV - anybody can use it until it runs out of electricity.

